objects.desc:
A concrete law for the fibres of a section, from the Law menu. Compression is negative, stresses in kN/m2, strains dimensionless.
Concrete01 - a parabola to the peak, a straight fall to the crushing strain, no tension (the default);
Concrete02 - the same with a tensile strength and a linear tension softening;
Concrete04 - Popovics' curve, and an exponential tension branch when you give fct and et.

A steel law for the fibres of a section, from the Law menu. Stresses in kN/m2, strains dimensionless.
Steel01 - bilinear with kinematic hardening (the default);
Steel02 - Giuffre-Menegotto-Pinto: the same, with a smooth elastic to plastic transition;
ReinforcingSteel - a reinforcing bar, with a strain-hardening branch to its ultimate strength.

